  "renderedGroups": [
    {
      "paragraph": 0,
      "speaker": "Narrator",
      "text": "Narrator:"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 0,
      "speaker": "Narrator",
      "text": " Rivermead School: facilities open to the public."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 1,
      "speaker": "Headteacher",
      "text": "Speaker:"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 1,
      "speaker": "Headteacher",
      "text": " I'd like to start by talking about the new theatre that we've just opened in our school. Its mission is to maximise opportunities for local audiences to experience productions of the highest quality."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 2,
      "speaker": "Headteacher",
      "text": "Speaker:"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 2,
      "speaker": "Headteacher",
      "text": " As well as music and dance there'll be drama from modern writers, and there'll also be a high proportion of shows aimed at children and families. You'll notice that there is one empty space in November — that's because the Chinese state acrobatic troupe have had to cancel their visit."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 3,
      "speaker": "Headteacher",
      "text": "Speaker:"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 3,
      "speaker": "Headteacher",
      "text": " Now, we're often asked about the theatre's sources of funding. Well, a limited amount of money will come from various government subsidies, but the bulk of the revenue will be generated by the sale of tickets, which is one reason why we'd be grateful for your help in promoting the work of the theatre."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 4,
      "speaker": "Headteacher",
      "text": "Speaker:"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 4,
      "speaker": "Headteacher",
      "text": " Entrance to the museum is free. We also have a state-of-the-art sports hall. This is reserved for our students during term time, but anyone can use it in the school holidays. And our cafeteria is worth a visit — it's open all day to visitors as well as to staff and students."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 5,
      "speaker": "Headteacher",
      "text": "Speaker:"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 5,
      "speaker": "Headteacher",
      "text": " First of all, the theatre — that's opposite car park P2, on the south side. You're not allowed to park anywhere except in the car parks."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 6,
      "speaker": "Headteacher",
      "text": "Speaker:"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 6,
      "speaker": "Headteacher",
      "text": " There are two marked on your map, P1 and P2, but there's a new car park which has only just been completed, and that's at the most northern end of the campus."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 7,
      "speaker": "Headteacher",
      "text": "Speaker:"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 7,
      "speaker": "Headteacher",
      "text": " Some people might want to consider coming by bus. There's a good service from the city centre to the school, and the bus stops at the roundabout — that's where it turns round to go back. It doesn't go up as far as Park Road."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 8,
      "speaker": "Headteacher",
      "text": "Speaker:"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 8,
      "speaker": "Headteacher",
      "text": " Then, to get to the sports hall you take the right fork after the main entrance and just keep going past the classroom block. You have to go straight across the roundabout, and it's further on, on the right-hand side of that road."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 9,
      "speaker": "Headteacher",
      "text": "Speaker:"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 9,
      "speaker": "Headteacher",
      "text": " Then there's the cafeteria. There are various ways to get there, because it's at the junction of Park Road and Rennie's Drive, on the north side of Park Road. In nice weather you can sit outside to eat and admire the view."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 10,
      "speaker": "Headteacher",
      "text": "Speaker:"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 10,
      "speaker": "Headteacher",
